<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
    SpotBugs + FindSecBugs exclusions.

    There are none. Reviewed false positives are suppressed in the source, on the exact method or
    field that triggers them, with @SuppressFBWarnings(value = "...", justification = "..."), so a
    new occurrence anywhere else is reported and has to be reviewed on its own. SpotBugs flags a
    suppression that no longer matches anything (US_USELESS_SUPPRESSION), which keeps them honest.

    Add an entry here only for a finding that cannot carry an annotation (for example in generated
    code), scoped with <Class> and <Method> (and <Field> where relevant), never by package, and with
    a comment saying why it is a false positive.
-->
<FindBugsFilter/>
